# Local Netlify folder
.netlify/*
!.netlify/functions-serve/
.netlify/functions-serve/*
!.netlify/functions-serve/package.json

# Same thing under src/. A pattern containing a slash is anchored to the directory
# holding this .gitignore, so the rules above only ever matched a top-level .netlify/
# and never src/.netlify/ — which is how 144 generated files (~80 MB) ended up tracked.
# Everything here is Netlify CLI state: netlify.toml points at src/netlify/functions
# (no dot) for real source.
src/.netlify/
node_modules
blog/_site/
blog-built/
blog/.jekyll-cache/
blog/.jekyll-metadata
.env
assets/videos/
old/
scratch_notes.txt
notes.txt
users/
